course: dictionary
lesson: 6277
title: Egg-laying mammals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mammal has fur or hair and feeds its babies milk. Most mammals give birth to live young, so you might think all mammals do. A monotreme is the surprise: it is a mammal that lays eggs instead of giving birth to live babies.
explain: «These egg-laying mammals are called monotremes: the platypus, with a duck-like bill, and four kinds of spiny echidna.» The clue is in the name: monotreme is a mammal that lays eggs, so when you see a monotreme, look for eggs.
explain: The platypus and the echidnas are the only living monotremes. Scientists find them special because they kept an old way of having babies that other mammals lost long ago.
fact: A monotreme is a mammal that lays eggs.
fact: Mammals have fur or hair and feed their babies milk.
fact: The platypus and the echidnas are the only living monotremes.
fact: Monotremes live only in Australia and New Guinea.
fact: «Monotremes kept an ancient way of having babies that the other mammals lost long ago.»
exercise: What is a monotreme? | A reptile that gives birth to live young | A bird that cannot fly | A fish that has fur | *A mammal that lays eggs
exercise: «The platypus, with a duck-like bill, is a monotreme.» Which animal is named as a monotreme? | A dolphin | A kangaroo | *The platypus
exercise: Why are monotremes a surprise? | They have feathers and can fly | *They are mammals, but they lay eggs | They are fish that climb trees
test: Is an echidna a monotreme? | *Yes, it is one of the only living monotremes | No, it gives birth to live young like most mammals | No, it is a bird
test: Which feature shows that an animal is a mammal? | Living only in water | Laying eggs | *Fur or hair
exam: Which statement about monotremes is correct? | They are birds that feed their babies milk | They give birth to live young, like all mammals | *They lay eggs, and the platypus and echidnas are the only living ones | They are found in every country in the world
